License of the data files this project publishes (the JSON under /dati)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
The published data files combine material under CC BY 4.0 (ISTAT, BDAP/SIOPE, Italia Domani,
OpenCoesione, IPA) with material under CC BY-SA 4.0 (ANAC). CC BY-SA requires that adapted
material be shared under the same license. So the DATA FILES published by this project are offered
under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), with the attributions below.
The source CODE stays MIT. Anyone reusing the published data must keep the attributions and share
their derived data under the same terms.

Data
----
- ISTAT (Italian National Institute of Statistics): municipal boundaries and resident
  population. License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
  https://www.istat.it

- BDAP / SIOPE, Ragioneria Generale dello Stato (Ministero dell'Economia e delle
  Finanze): monthly cumulative cash receipts and payments of every Italian municipality,
  by item of the chart of accounts. Published as open data under Creative Commons
  Attribution (CC BY) in the BDAP open data catalogue.
  https://bdap-opendata.rgs.mef.gov.it

- MEF - Dipartimento delle Finanze (Ministry of Economy and Finance, Department of Finance):
  "Redditi e principali variabili IRPEF su base comunale", tax declarations aggregated by
  municipality and tax year (taxable income, number of taxpayers, municipal surtax).
  https://www1.finanze.gov.it/finanze/analisi_stat/public/index.php?opendata=yes
  The portal's "license type" field is empty. Under art. 52 of the Italian Digital Administration
  Code (CAD), public data published without an explicit license are open data by default; we cite the
  source on the site. Cells with few taxpayers are hidden by the publisher for statistical secrecy:
  they are kept as NULL, never as zero.

- Italia Domani (PNRR Mission Structure, via Sogei): "Progetti del PNRR", all projects of the national
  recovery plan, CC BY 4.0. https://www.italiadomani.gov.it/content/sogei-ng/it/it/catalogo-open-data.html
  The file does not locate projects: a project is attributed to a municipality only when the municipality
  itself is the implementing body.

- OpenCoesione (Italian Department for Cohesion Policy): all projects financed by cohesion policies
  (2000-2027), CC BY 4.0. https://opencoesione.gov.it/it/opendata/
  Only projects located in a single municipality are used. Names of private companies and persons
  receiving incentives or grants are never published.

- ANAC - Autorita' Nazionale Anticorruzione, Banca dati nazionale dei contratti pubblici: lots (CIG) of
  public tenders (2020-2025) and their awards (number of bids and discount only; the names of the winning
  companies are not used). License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0).
  https://dati.anticorruzione.it/opendata  - Only lots tendered by a municipality itself are used.
  The declared lot value is NOT summed blindly: adhesions to framework agreements report the agreement's
  ceiling, and some values are typing errors (e.g. 1.1 billion euro of meal vouchers for a town of 12,000
  people). See db/migrations/20261003300000_appalti.sql.

- IPA - Indice delle Pubbliche Amministrazioni (AgID), CC BY 4.0: used only to match an implementing
  body's fiscal code to its municipality; none of its content is republished.

These are CASH accounting figures (money actually collected and paid), not accrual
accounting (accertamenti / impegni). They do not match a municipality's official
rendiconto.

Base map
--------
- Map tiles and style: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, (c) CARTO. The default basemap
